│ patch_name               │ reduce_regularization_increase_expressivity                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The model predictions have collapsed toward the mean, indicated by a very low             │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio (0.0091), meaning the model is not learning meaningful signal and is       │
│                          │ outputting near-constant predictions. The warning suggests increasing model expressivity  │
│                          │ or reducing regularization.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The root cause is overly strong regularization and possibly too few estimators or too low │
│                          │ learning rate. The current parameters have min_child_weight=10, reg_alpha=0.1,            │
│                          │ reg_lambda=1.0, subsample=0.6, colsample_bytree=0.8, and learning_rate=0.01 with 300      │
│                          │ estimators.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To fix this, I will:                                                                      │
│                          │ - Reduce min_child_weight from 10 to 1 (less strict leaf size)                            │
│                          │ - Reduce reg_alpha from 0.1 to 0 (less L1 regularization)                                 │
│                          │ - Reduce reg_lambda from 1.0 to 0.5 (less L2 regularization)                              │
│                          │ - Increase subsample to 0.8 (more data per tree)                                          │
│                          │ - Increase learning_rate to 0.05 (faster learning)                                        │
│                          │ - Increase n_estimators to 500 (more trees to learn signal)                               │
│                          │ - Keep max_depth=4 to avoid overfitting                                                   │
│                          │ - Keep early_stopping_rounds=30 to prevent overfitting                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes should increase model expressivity and reduce regularization, allowing the  │
│                          │ model to learn meaningful patterns and avoid collapsing predictions.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ No changes to feature engineering or other code are needed.                               │
