│ patch_name               │ reduce_regularization_increase_expressivity                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The model predictions are collapsing toward the mean with a very low prediction standard  │
│                          │ deviation ratio (0.0091, well below threshold 0.15), indicating underfitting and          │
│                          │ over-regularization with insufficient model expressivity. The current hyperparameters use │
│                          │ very strong regularization: min_child_weight=10, reg_alpha=0.1, learning_rate=0.01,       │
│                          │ n_estimators=300.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To fix this, I reduced regularization by lowering min_child_weight to 1, setting          │
│                          │ reg_alpha to 0 (no L1), increased learning rate to 0.05 for faster learning, and          │
│                          │ decreased n_estimators to 100 to prevent prolonged weak training. These changes should    │
│                          │ help the model find stronger signals and output a more diverse prediction distribution,   │
│                          │ raising pred_std_ratio above threshold and improving validation directional accuracy.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ No changes were needed in feature engineering (which is rich and time-correct), or        │
│                          │ clipping constants. The rest of the code remains unchanged to keep the interface stable.  │
