╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_model_collapse_add_features_loosen_reg                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The primary issue is that the model's predictions have collapsed toward the mean,         │
│                          │ indicated by a very low pred_std_ratio (~0.018), which means the model is not learning to │
│                          │ differentiate signals well, just outputting near-constant predictions. This causes poor   │
│                          │ directional accuracy reliability. The warning suggests increasing model expressivity or   │
│                          │ adding more signal features, or loosening regularization.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ In the current code, although some attempts to loosen regularization were made            │
│                          │ (min_child_weight=1, reg_alpha=0.0, reg_lambda=0.5), the model's fit still collapses. One │
│                          │ likely cause is the feature matrix after dropna() removes many rows due to lookbacks,     │
│                          │ leading to data leakage risks or poor generalization. Also, the "returns" features are    │
│                          │ computed with pct_change but not shifted forward; as the task forbids using future data,  │
│                          │ we must shift features by at least 1 to avoid lookahead bias.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Here is the fix approach:                                                                 │
│                          │ - Shift all features by 1 to ensure only past data is used.                               │
│                          │ - Add additional simple momentum and volatility features, including short and medium      │
│                          │ rolling means of returns, and normalize features to improve signal.                       │
│                          │ - Prevent leakage and keep total feature count below 80.                                  │
│                          │ - Loosen regularization slightly by increasing learning rate and reducing n_estimators to │
