│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_loosen_regularization                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The error message indicates that the model's predictions have collapsed toward the mean,  │
│                          │ evidenced by a very low pred_std_ratio (0.0091), which is far below the minimum           │
│                          │ acceptable 0.15. This suggests the model is underfitting and overly regularized, causing  │
│                          │ it to predict near the mean rather than capturing signal. The current hyperparameters     │
│                          │ have strong regularization (min_child_weight=10, reg_alpha=0.1, subsample=0.6) and a low  │
│                          │ learning rate (0.01) with many estimators (300), which can cause this collapse.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To fix this, I loosened regularization by reducing min_child_weight from 10 to 1, reduced │
│                          │ reg_alpha from 0.1 to 0.0, increased subsample from 0.6 to 0.8, and increased             │
│                          │ learning_rate from 0.01 to 0.05 to allow faster learning and more expressivity. I also    │
│                          │ reduced n_estimators from 300 to 150 to keep training time reasonable with the higher     │
│                          │ learning rate. These changes should increase model expressivity and prevent prediction    │
│                          │ collapse while maintaining reasonable training time.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ No changes were made to feature engineering or other parts, as the main issue is model    │
│                          │ underfitting due to excessive regularization and low learning rate.                       │
