│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_with_feature_and_param_adjustments                                │
│ patch_description        │ The model predictions are collapsing toward the mean, indicated by a very low             │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio (~0.006), despite increased model complexity and added polynomial          │
│                          │ features. This suggests the model is under-expressive or overly regularized, or the       │
│                          │ features do not provide enough signal variance. The root cause is likely that the         │
│                          │ features are overly smoothed or shifted too aggressively, reducing signal variance, and   │
│                          │ the model parameters (especially reg_lambda=1.0) still impose too much regularization.    │
│                          │ Also, the target clipping at 95th percentile may reduce target variance too much.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fixes applied:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Reduced feature shifting to only 1 bar lag where necessary, avoiding double shifts that │
│                          │ overly smooth features.                                                                   │
│                          │ - Removed StandardScaler inside build_features to avoid leaking info and double scaling   │
│                          │ (scaling is done in run_experiment).                                                      │
│                          │ - Reduced reg_lambda from 1.0 to 0.0 to remove L2 regularization and increase model       │
│                          │ expressivity.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Increased learning_rate to 0.1 for faster fitting.                                      │
│                          │ - Increased max_depth to 8 to allow more complex trees.                                   │
│                          │ - Increased subsample and colsample_bytree to 0.9 to use more data/features per tree.     │
│                          │ - Increased CLIP_PERCENTILE to 99 to keep more target variance.                           │
│                          │ - Added a small epsilon in divisions to avoid NaNs.                                       │
│                          │ - Ensured all features are shifted by exactly 1 bar to prevent lookahead but preserve     │
│                          │ variance.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Removed polynomial feature scaling inside build_features to avoid double scaling and    │
│                          │ potential leakage.                                                                        │
│                          │ - Added a few additional momentum and volatility features with minimal lag to increase    │
│                          │ signal.                                                                                   │
│                          │ These changes increase model expressivity and feature signal variance, addressing the     │
│                          │ collapse warning and improving pred_std_ratio.                                            │
