│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_increase_expressivity                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The primary issue is the model predictions collapsing toward the mean, evidenced by the   │
│                          │ very low pred_std_ratio (~0.006). This means the model is effectively outputting nearly   │
│                          │ constant predictions with little variance, failing to leverage the input data's signal.   │
│                          │ The error suggests increasing model expressivity or removing regularization.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current fix from the previous iteration loosened min_child_weight and removed L1      │
│                          │ regularization but increased learning rate only moderately and kept a low max_depth,      │
│                          │ which still restricts model complexity. This leads to underfitting.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To fix this, I restore a more permissive max_depth and reduce regularization further, and │
│                          │ increase learning rate more to allow better fitting. Also, adding early stopping on       │
│                          │ validation will prevent overfitting. Additionally, changing the early stopping to watch   │
│                          │ the validation set ('val') not just 'test' might help, but as per instructions, I leave   │
│                          │ run_experiment unchanged except for param adjustments.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ No feature code changes, just hyperparameters to increase model expressivity:             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - max_depth: increase from 4 to 6 (more complex trees)                                    │
│                          │ - min_child_weight: keep at 1 (looser than original 10)                                   │
│                          │ - reg_alpha: 0.0 (no L1)                                                                  │
│                          │ - reg_lambda: reduced to 0.5 to reduce L2 regularization                                  │
│                          │ - learning_rate: increased to 0.1 for faster learning                                     │
│                          │ - n_estimators: keep 300                                                                  │
│                          │ - keep other params unchanged                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help the model produce predictions with higher variance and escape the mean   │
│                          │ collapse.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I keep features and everything else the same.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The code changes are only in the XGB_PARAMS block.                                        │
