│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_add_momentum_features_and_adjust_hyperparams                      │
│ patch_description        │ The main issue is that the model's predictions collapse toward the mean, indicated by a   │
│                          │ very low pred_std_ratio (~0.018), meaning the model is not capturing enough signal and is │
│                          │ essentially predicting near the mean target. This suggests insufficient model             │
│                          │ expressivity or lack of informative features.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior attempts shows that adding momentum features shifted by 1 (to avoid     │
│                          │ lookahead) helped increase expressivity and reduce collapse warnings. The current program │
│                          │ lacks these momentum features, which likely reduces signal strength.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the current hyperparameters use a high learning rate (0.1) with no          │
│                          │ regularization and full subsample/colsample, which can cause unstable training or         │
│                          │ overfitting, but here the problem is under-expressivity (collapse), so we should reduce   │
│                          │ learning rate slightly and loosen regularization minimally.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix:                                                                                      │
│                          │ - Add momentum features (momentum_5 and momentum_10) shifted by 1 to build_features().    │
│                          │ - Reduce learning_rate from 0.1 to 0.05 for more stable training.                         │
│                          │ - Loosen min_child_weight from 1 to 0.5 to allow more splits.                             │
│                          │ - Keep reg_alpha=0.0 to avoid L1 regularization but keep reg_lambda=1.0.                  │
│                          │ - Keep subsample and colsample_bytree at 1.0 to maximize data and features per tree.      │
│                          │ - Keep n_estimators=200 to keep training time reasonable.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes increase model expressivity and add signal features, addressing the         │
│                          │ collapse warning and improving pred_std_ratio and directional accuracy.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All features remain shifted properly to avoid lookahead bias, and total feature count     │
│                          │ remains under 80.                                                                         │
