│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_increase_expressivity_and_correct_shifts                          │
│ patch_description        │ The main issue is that the model's predictions collapse toward the mean, indicated by a   │
│                          │ very low pred_std_ratio (~0.01), meaning the model is not expressive enough or is         │
│                          │ over-regularized. The current hyperparameters still have some regularization              │
│                          │ (reg_lambda=0.5) and relatively shallow depth (max_depth=5), which may limit              │
│                          │ expressivity. Also, the feature engineering applies many shifts, but some features like   │
│                          │ 'atr_norm' and 'vol_regime' are not fully shifted, potentially leaking future info or     │
│                          │ causing misalignment.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fixes applied:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Increase model expressivity by raising max_depth to 7 and removing regularization       │
│                          │ (reg_alpha=0, reg_lambda=0).                                                              │
│                          │ - Increase n_estimators to 600 to allow more boosting rounds.                             │
│                          │ - Reduce learning_rate to 0.03 for stable training with more estimators.                  │
│                          │ - Ensure all features use only past data by shifting all features consistently by 1 bar,  │
│                          │ including 'atr_norm' and 'vol_regime'.                                                    │
│                          │ - Shift 'atr_norm' and 'vol_regime' by 1 to avoid lookahead.                              │
│                          │ - Shift 'vwap_dev' and volume ratios are already shifted.                                 │
│                          │ - Keep the rest of the feature engineering consistent with past data only.                │
│                          │ - These changes should increase model expressivity and prevent prediction collapse while  │
│                          │ respecting constraints.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This addresses the warning about collapsed predictions and should improve pred_std_ratio  │
│                          │ above the 0.15 threshold, fixing the validation failure.                                  │
