├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_remove_shift_and_add_features                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The main issue causing prediction collapse (very low pred_std_ratio ~0.01) is overly      │
│                          │ cautious feature shifting, which removes too much useful signal, and not enough model     │
│                          │ expressivity or informative features to allow non-trivial predictions. This causes the    │
│                          │ model to regress heavily to the mean.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The program attempts to avoid lookahead by shifting nearly all features by 1 but applied  │
│                          │ shifts inside rolling calculations leading to effectively stale info and low signal       │
│                          │ variance.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fixes applied:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Remove unnecessary shifting inside rolling computations where it causes data to lag     │
│                          │ excessively.                                                                              │
│                          │ - Apply only one final shift for all features after computation where needed to ensure no │
│                          │ lookahead.                                                                                │
│                          │ - Add a few more expressive features (momentum and volume related) without shift loss.    │
│                          │ - Maintain past-only data usage but avoid compounding shifts that reduce signal.          │
│                          │ - Keep model hyperparameters as is to allow enough expressivity (max_depth=5,             │
│                          │ learning_rate=0.05).                                                                      │
│                          │ - These changes restore signal diversity and avoid mean collapse, improving               │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio without inducing overfit.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This fix addresses the root cause shown by warnings and low pred_std_ratio through better │
│                          │ feature construction.                                                                     │
