│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_feature_shift_and_increase_model_expressivity                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The main issue causing the model to collapse predictions toward the mean (very low        │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio) is excessive regularization and insufficient model expressivity. The      │
│                          │ current model uses moderate regularization and moderate tree depth but still collapses.   │
│                          │ Additionally, the feature engineering applies shifts to all features, which is correct to │
│                          │ avoid lookahead, but the time-based features use a frequency string '15min' which is      │
│                          │ correct, but the orderbook features are shifted after applying df.apply, which can cause  │
│                          │ misalignment or NaNs.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To fix:                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Increase model expressivity by increasing max_depth and reducing regularization        │
│                          │ (reg_lambda), and increasing n_estimators slightly, while keeping early stopping.         │
│                          │ 2. Fix feature engineering to shift orderbook features before applying the lambda to      │
│                          │ avoid misalignment and ensure no lookahead.                                               │
│                          │ 3. Add a few interaction features to increase signal without increasing feature count too │
│                          │ much.                                                                                     │
│                          │ 4. Keep all features shifted by 1 to avoid lookahead, but ensure the shifting is          │
│                          │ consistent and no NaNs are introduced unnecessarily.                                      │
│                          │ 5. Add normalization to features to help model training.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes address the collapse warning by increasing model capacity and ensuring      │
│                          │ features are properly aligned without lookahead.                                          │
